# The safe-state watchdog for Automation device grants. It runs on
# central_server_pc next to the Control Center, as the same Windows account.
# Copy to C:\ProgramData\LabNet\watchdog.env.
# Start by hand:
#   C:\ProgramData\LabNet\control-center-venv\Scripts\labnet-watchdog.exe --env-file C:\ProgramData\LabNet\watchdog.env
#
# If the Control Center dies or hangs while a grant holds devices, the watchdog
# waits for its leases to lapse, takes them with its own Central user, applies
# the approved protocol's safe state and releases them (see packages/labnet/README.md,
# "The safe-state watchdog").
#
# Start from the file `labnet-central-admin setup --user automation-watchdog
# --write-env ... --server-url http://127.0.0.1:8008` made: it already holds
# the two Central settings below. Its own user, never the Control Center's key.
# Development uses the same layout in .devnet/automation-watchdog.env (written
# by labnet dev seed).

# Central on this same computer, over loopback.
LABNET_SERVER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8008
LABNET_API_KEY=<from setup --write-env>
# Set LABNET_CA_FILE exactly as in control-center.env, if it is set there.
# LABNET_CA_FILE=C:/ProgramData/LabNet/certs/labnet-ca.pem

# The Control Center's Automation folder: its LABNET_AUTOMATION_DIR. The
# watchdog reads the grant records in state\ and writes only its own claim
# files and audit lines there.
LABNET_AUTOMATION_DIR=C:\ProgramData\LabNet\automation

# The Control Center's built-in server (its /health/live is checked).
# LABNET_WATCHDOG_CONTROL_CENTER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080

# The watchdog's own health page, loopback only:
# http://127.0.0.1:8081/health/ready. One watchdog per computer: a second one
# can't take the port and exits.
# LABNET_WATCHDOG_PORT=8081

# Timing (defaults shown). A grant is taken over when its heartbeat is
# STALE_SECONDS old and the Control Center hasn't answered for as long (or
# answers while the heartbeat stays stale twice as long: a hung event loop).
# Central is asked for the leases for up to LEASE_WAIT_SECONDS (at least 60,
# Central's lease length). A grant with no heartbeat for MAX_AGE_MINUTES is
# never acted on, only logged: check its devices by hand.
# LABNET_WATCHDOG_STALE_SECONDS=20
# LABNET_WATCHDOG_POLL_SECONDS=2
# LABNET_WATCHDOG_LEASE_WAIT_SECONDS=120
# LABNET_WATCHDOG_MAX_AGE_MINUTES=60
